{
 "title": "What's inside an iPhone? \u2014 c10-parts",
 "voice": "am_puck",
 "speed": 0.96,
 "segments": [
  {
   "text": "Can you repair an iPhone with any spare part?",
   "scene": true,
   "split": [
    4
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Technically, yes.",
   "scene": true
  },
  {
   "text": "But your iPhone will notice."
  },
  {
   "text": "The battery, the screen, the cameras and the logic board",
   "scene": true,
   "split": [
    3,
    6
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "are all tracked."
  },
  {
   "text": "Put in a part that's not genuine,",
   "scene": true
  },
  {
   "text": "and Settings says:",
   "pause": 0.15
  },
  {
   "text": "Unknown Part."
  },
  {
   "text": "You get a notification when you unlock it...",
   "scene": true,
   "split": [
    3
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "and another one five days later."
  },
  {
   "text": "Just in case you forgot."
  },
  {
   "text": "Even genuine parts must be calibrated,",
   "scene": true
  },
  {
   "text": "with data stored on Apple's servers."
  },
  {
   "text": "Apple says it's about quality and security.",
   "scene": true,
   "split": [
    3
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Critics say it's about control."
  },
  {
   "text": "Either way:",
   "scene": true,
   "pause": 0.15
  },
  {
   "text": "your battery has a passport."
  }
 ]
}